{
  "comment": "Requests that a recorder sends to the real TCO policies API, and the offline test sends to the fake. Paths are relative to /dataplans. The recorder first saves the log, span, and RUM policies of the tenant, and puts them back at the end (with new ids); it stops before any write when it cannot read one of them. Bodies are the ones that the released resources send. Ids, companyId, createdAt, and updatedAt are masked.",
